 "notes": "Roland and Stuckey, SIR 2019-5094 version 1.1 (which changed a source citation in Table 2, not the equations): five flood-flow regions at 8 AEPs from Table 3, with AVP and SEP; ranges from Table 5. Equation 4 adds 0.1 to the percentages, so CARBON and STORAGE have offset 0.1. The report prints no covariance or model error variance, so intervals use the AVP. NSS's maximum DRNAREA for region 2 is 1,160 mi2 where Table 5 prints 1,610; appendix 1 has a region 2 gage above 1,160, so this file has 1,610. NSS also has region 2's 4-percent STORAGE coefficient as -0.0831 where Table 3 prints -0.0813, and SEPs of 28.9 percent (region 2, 10 percent) and 32.2 percent (region 5, 1 percent) where Table 3 prints 28.19 and 33.2. Appendix 2's regression flows reproduce from appendix 1's characteristics at all 285 gages used in the regressions, which confirms -0.0813.",
